---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`About ${site.name}, machine learning engineer and researcher.`}>
  <section class="page-intro shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>From communication systems to machine learning.</h1>
    <div class="intro-columns">
      <p class="lede">Telecommunications taught me to look at the whole system: the signal, the network, and what can fail between them.</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>I studied communication and electrical engineering at Beirut Arab University, then saw those ideas in practice during a telecommunications internship at OGERO. Working around access networks, fiber, and mobile systems made reliability and physical constraints concrete.</p>
        <p>My UAV GPS spoofing project brought me into machine learning through a familiar problem: deciding whether a signal can be trusted. A football forecasting project taught me a different lesson about time-aware data, leakage, and the uncertainty that remains even after careful modeling.</p>
        <p>At the American University of Beirut, I moved deeper into how models learn. My master’s thesis studied adaptive optimization under differential privacy and how training decisions affect underrepresented groups.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">What comes next</p>
      <p class="section-note">The questions connecting my engineering and research work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="intro-columns about-direction">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Problems that interest me</h2>
        <p>I’m drawn to systems that must make useful decisions from noisy or sensitive data, especially when accuracy alone hides security risks, privacy costs, or uneven outcomes across groups.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Where I’m headed</h2>
        <p>I want to bring this systems perspective to applied machine learning: build models that respect privacy and resource limits, test them beyond a single headline metric, and make their failure modes understandable.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
